PURPOSE: Checks on shell tool use. Verified one-by-one at finish (lenient if shell was not used).
001. Each shell command carried a reason, expected result, destructive-risk answer, and timeout.
002. Commands were narrow rather than broad, and never used sudo or host-modifying actions.
003. Exit code, stdout, and stderr were inspected before the next step.
004. A failed command was fixed and re-run, or the failure was reported — not ignored.
